From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 13:05:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: Trackpad Keys or Pointer in Settings > Keyboard

The Zinwa Q25 trackpad has two modes in the bbqX0kbd driver: arrow keys
(the default, BlackBerry focus movement) and a pointer. Settings >
System > Keyboard > Trackpad offers both. Settings only stores the
choice in persist.sys.sable.trackpad (keys or pointer); init writes the
driver's /proc/q20_switch_key_mouse from it (sable-trackpad.rc), which
device patch 1503 labels so no app can write it. Shown only where the
switch exists.
---
 res/values/sable_trackpad_strings.xml         | 35 +++++++++
 res/xml/keyboard_settings.xml                 | 11 +++
 .../SableTrackpadPreferenceController.java    | 76 +++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 122 insertions(+)

diff --git a/res/values/sable_trackpad_strings.xml b/res/values/sable_trackpad_strings.xml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9fff106
--- /dev/null
+++ b/res/values/sable_trackpad_strings.xml
@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
